            <ArticleTitle>Withdrawal phenomenon after abrupt cessation of nifedipine in stable angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>298-301</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We investigated the effect of abrupt cessation of nifedipine after regular administration (20 mg, four times daily) for 5 weeks in seven patients with stable angina pectoris. A rebound decrease in exercise tolerance and increase of exercise-induced myocardial ischaemia were registered on the first day of nifedipine withdrawal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
